---
import "../styles/global.css";

const title = "Prosary — Privacy Policy";
const description =
  "Prosary's privacy policy: no analytics, no ads, no accounts in the apps; the only network feature is the optional community devotion repository, and the prayers.prosary.app service stores only what an account needs.";
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<meta name="description" content={description} />
		<title>{title}</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="hero">
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="tagline">Last updated: 2026-08-01</p>
		</div>

		<section>
			<p>
				Prosary is a Catholic prayer companion, available for iPhone, Mac,
				Android, and (in development) Windows, alongside two web services:
				<a href="https://compose.prosary.app">Prosary Compose</a> for
				authoring devotions and
				<a href="https://prayers.prosary.app">Prosary Prayers</a>, the
				community devotion repository. This policy covers all of them.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>The apps</h2>
			<p>
				The apps have no accounts, no sign-in, no analytics, no crash
				reporting, no advertising, and no third-party SDKs. Your saved
				prayer favorites and reminder times live in a local database on
				your device (SwiftData on iPhone/Mac, Room on Android, SQLite on
				Windows).
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>iCloud sync (Apple devices).</strong> On iPhone and Mac,
					your favorites and any devotion bundles you import sync between
					your own devices through your personal iCloud account (Apple's
					CloudKit and iCloud Drive). This data stays inside your private
					iCloud storage — it is never sent to us, and we cannot read it.
					Signing out of iCloud keeps everything working locally.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>The community repository (the one network feature).</strong>
					The Browse and Search tabs can fetch the public devotion catalog
					from prayers.prosary.app and download bundles you choose to
					install. These requests carry the technical information every web
					request carries (such as your IP address), processed transiently
					by our hosting to serve the request; each download also increments
					an anonymous per-bundle counter. No account, identifier, or
					tracking of any kind is attached, and if you never open those
					tabs, the apps make no network requests at all.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Notifications</h2>
			<p>
				Prayer reminders you configure are scheduled entirely on your device
				(via <code>UNUserNotificationCenter</code> on iPhone/Mac,
				<code>AlarmManager</code> on Android, or scheduled toasts on
				Windows) and shown as local notifications. No reminder data ever
				leaves your device.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Permissions</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Notifications</strong> — used only to show the prayer
					reminders you configure.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Internet</strong> (Android lists this explicitly) — used
					only by the community repository browser described above.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Receive boot completed</strong> (Android only) — used only
					to re-schedule your existing reminders after your device restarts,
					since Android clears scheduled alarms on reboot.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>No permission is used to collect or transmit personal data.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Prosary Compose (compose.prosary.app)</h2>
			<p>
				Compose runs entirely in your browser: the devotions you write, the
				artwork you attach, and the bundles you build never leave your
				device. Work-in-progress is autosaved to your browser's local
				storage on your own machine. Compose has no accounts, no analytics,
				and sets no cookies.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Prosary Prayers (prayers.prosary.app)</h2>
			<p>
				Browsing and downloading from the repository requires no account.
				If you create one to publish devotions, we store only what the
				service needs:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Username</strong> — public; it names your published
					bundles (<code>repo.&lt;username&gt;.…</code>).
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Passkey public keys</strong> — sign-in uses passkeys;
					there are no passwords, and biometric data never leaves your
					device (we receive only the public key your device creates).
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Recovery email address</strong> — stored privately and
					used for exactly one thing: sending account-recovery links (via
					Brevo, our email processor). It is never displayed, shared, or
					used for marketing.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Published bundles</strong> — public by design: the
					devotion, its name, description, tags, and your username are
					visible to everyone, in the apps and on the site. You can remove
					your bundles from your account page at any time.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>A session cookie</strong> — strictly functional (it keeps
					you signed in for up to 30 days); there are no tracking or
					third-party cookies.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Download counts are anonymous aggregates per bundle. Account data
				and bundles are stored on our hosting providers' infrastructure
				(Vercel and Neon, EU region). To delete your account entirely,
				email us — removal of your bundles is self-serve, and account
				deletion is handled on request until a self-serve control ships.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Hosting</h2>
			<p>
				prosary.app is served by GitHub Pages; compose.prosary.app and
				prayers.prosary.app are served by Vercel. Like virtually all web
				hosts, these providers process standard technical request data
				(such as IP addresses) transiently to deliver the sites and keep
				them secure. We run no analytics on any of them.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				If this policy changes, the "Last updated" date above will change
				accordingly.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about this policy can be sent to
				<a href="mailto:mail@dkaluta.com">mail@dkaluta.com</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<footer>
			<p>
				&copy; 2026 David Kaluta &middot; <a href="/">Home</a> &middot;
				<a href="/license">License</a>
			</p>
		</footer>
	</body>
</html>
